# The Arabic-borrowed plural for a DURATION of hours, resting on the native
# Kabyle speaker @athmanemokraoui alone.  On
# https://github.com/TigreGotico/chronologia/pull/846#issuecomment-5573978767:
#   "'ssaɛtin' means only two o'clock.  A duration of two hours is 'snat n
#    sswayeɛ'."
# So "snat n sswayeɛ" is two hours, and the clock hour "ssaɛtin" is
# deliberately absent from this file.
sswayeɛ
